module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.gunbc_run_pays_a_large_fixed_pre_entry_cost_per_invocation

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data gunbc_run_pays_a_large_fixed_pre_entry_cost_per_invocation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "gunbc_run_pays_a_large_fixed_pre_entry_cost_per_invocation" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**every `gunbc run` step pays a fixed per-invocation cost that does not scale with its entry's closure** (INVALID STATE: a CI step whose work is a few-module fold -- read one environment variable, compare it to one host name -- costs minutes of wall time before it evaluates anything, and the cost is denominated in the corpus rather than in the entry. A step budget sized for the fold is then consumed by work the fold never demanded.)",
    "HARM. Every fleet-converge and floor step that shells `gunbc run` pays it on every dispatch, so it multiplies across steps and runs. It also hides closure cost: a step that times out cannot be told apart, from its budget alone, from a step whose entry closure grew. Run 36170715248 timed out at 'Mt. Collins boot admission (credential-free)' on a combination of both.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. This is not the closure-size defect that run exhibited. Moving the admission fold into its own module (gunbc#12311, gunbc.machine_intake_mtcollins1_boot_admission) removed the typecheck of the boot run's closure, and the same measurement fell substantially. It did not fall toward zero: the remainder is paid identically for a closure of three modules and printed no typecheck lines. So the residue is a fixed cost paid before the entry is resolved -- that much is measured. WHAT it is remains a HYPOTHESIS (DESIGN §4d): whole-tree preparation is the leading candidate, not an established cause, and this row is named for the measured fact so that confirming or refuting the hypothesis does not rename it.",
    "INSTRUMENT (DESIGN §6: named here, its figures deliberately not transcribed): `time FLEET_CONVERGE_EXPECTED_HOST=srv1 gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/machine_intake/mtcollins1_boot_admission.dag --function mtcollins1_boot_admit_executor` on a head-built gunbc, compared with the same function under the larger entry that held it before gunbc#12311. The row claims the comparison's SHAPE -- the small entry is much cheaper than the large one and still far from free -- and a reader re-derives the magnitudes rather than reading them here.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the shared gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes bounds the step, and the step refuses at its budget rather than running unbounded.",
    "CEILING: mechanically preventable. A gate can hold each gunbc run step's measured wall time against a cost derived from its entry closure. Whether the fixed part can be removed entirely depends on what the preparation computes, which is not yet decomposed.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a decomposition of `gunbc run`'s pre-entry preparation into named phases with their own costs, sufficient to show which part a small-closure entry does not demand. Until then, a step timeout derived from closure cost has no fixed-cost term to add.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fleet_workflow_steps", decl_name: "gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.ci_spec", decl_name: "gunbc_ci_mtcollins1_boot_admit_target", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
